      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# H3 Music Video - masked audio, written locally by Ollama\n\nThe song is the clock. The writer cuts it into 5-15 s pieces on the music (timed\nlyrics make cuts land before a line), writes one H3 scene per piece, and emits\nmatching lists - `scenes`, `lengths`, `audio_segments`, `clip_starts` - that the\nvideo node renders one clip at a time.\n\n**Masked audio** is what makes the lip-sync work: each clip's real slice of the\nsong is encoded and written straight into the H3 audio latent with the mask held\nat 0, so the model generates picture against a frozen, real vocal instead of being\nasked politely to sync. That is why the song is *not* wired to `ref_audio`.\n\n**What is different here:** the scenes are written by a local model. The **Ollama\nbackend** node overrides the writer's `model` dropdown - the Claude Code CLI is\nnever called, no API key is needed, nothing leaves this machine. The writer is **blind**: the performer photo goes to the video model only, so this runs on any text model - no vision required.\n\n**Output:** every piece is decoded and saved as its own file by H3 Save Clip,\ncarrying its original slice of the song. Stitch them externally, or add\n**H3 Scenes Join** with `replace_audio` = the LoadAudio output for one file with\nthe full mix.\n\n**Seed:** the writer's seed is -1 (randomize) - every queue writes a brand-new\nvideo. Set a fixed number to re-render the same scenes.\n"
      ],
      "title": "How this works",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
