    {
      "id": 195,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -2600,
        5510
      ],
      "size": [
        700,
        940
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "title": "Ollama setup",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Ollama setup - read this first\n\nThe whole video is written by **ollama:qwen3.8:27b** on this machine. Nothing is sent anywhere.\n\n```\nollama pull qwen3.8:27b\nollama serve\n```\n\nThen reload the ComfyUI page so the backend node can see the model.\n\n## num_ctx is the setting that matters\n\nThe H3 system prompt is **9k tokens** (text-only) to **15k tokens** (with reference\nimages) before your song, cast and lyrics are added. Ollama picks its own context\nfrom free VRAM - as little as 4k - and **silently truncates** everything past it,\nstarting with the rules the model is supposed to follow. The result is not an\nerror, it is a bad prompt.\n\nThe **Ollama backend** node sets `num_ctx` explicitly (32768 here). Press\n**📏 Show 1024 tokens** on that node to see what a token actually is, what an H3\nrun spends, and how much context fits in this machine's VRAM and RAM.\n\n## The other two settings\n\n- **thinking = off.** qwen3.8 reasons before answering by default. The H3 rules are\n  already in the system prompt, so the reasoning is pure wall-clock cost. Any\n  `<think>` block that does arrive is stripped before parsing either way.\n- **scenes_per_call = 2, parallel_chunks = off.** One local model, one GPU: four\n  concurrent chunks just queue behind each other. Small serial chunks finish inside\n  the timeout and each one keeps the whole conversation in context.\n  (`parallel_chunks = on` only pays off with `OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL` raised.)\n\n## Local-model tips\n\n- Keep **locations** to one or two entries. The continuity pass asks the model to\n  honour every location anchor in every scene, and a local model will obey too\n  literally - cramming all of them into one shot.\n- Give the performer a **name** in `extra_cast` (\"Lead singer: Mara, ...\").\n  Without one the model invents a new name for them in each chunk.\n- A 27B model at Q4 takes ~20-40 s per scene chunk. A 3-minute song is\n  ~18 pieces, so budget 5-10 minutes for the writing pass.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": 196,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -2600,
        6500
      ],
      "size": [
        700,
        520
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "title": "Blind Ref2VA - how this works",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Blind Ref2VA - reference photos on a model that cannot see\n\nThis is the middle setting between the other two Ollama workflows, and for local\nmodels it is usually the right one.\n\n- The **video model** still receives the photo as `<Picture 1>`, exactly as in a\n  normal Ref2VA run - the render is identical.\n- The **writer** never receives a single pixel. It learns who is in each picture\n  from the cast line and from `image_notes`, and binds the label by position:\n  `<Subject 1> Mara (S1) <Picture 1>, a woman in her early 30s with a platinum\n  pixie cut, wearing ...`\n\nThat means **any text model works** - a plain `qwen3`, a small quantised model, an\nuncensored fine-tune - and you still get face consistency across every clip,\nbecause face consistency comes from the picture reaching the *video* model, not\nfrom the writer having looked at it.\n\n## What you must write\n\n`image_notes` is doing the work here. One line per picture:\n\n```\nImage 1: Mara, the lead singer\nImage 2: the diner, use as the location\n```\n\nA picture with no note is bound to the cast member in the same position in cast\norder. The writer is explicitly forbidden from describing or guessing at picture\ncontents, so anything you do not state it will take from the CAST lines and the\nwardrobe lock instead - keep those specific.\n\n## Cost\n\nBlind Ref2VA uses the reference guide, so the system prompt is ~15k tokens rather\nthan the ~9k of a text-only FL run - but it sends **no image data at all**, which\non a local model is usually the bigger saving. `num_ctx` 32768 covers it.\n\n## The three Ollama workflows\n\n| Workflow | Writer sees photo | Video model gets photo | Needs vision |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `..._ollama.json` (Ref2VA) | yes | yes | **yes** |\n| `..._ollama_blindref.json` (this one) | no | yes | no |\n| `..._ollama_textonly.json` (FL / T2VA) | no | no | no |\n"
      ],
      "color": "#2a3f4a",
      "bgcolor": "#1b2b33",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": []
    },
